{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009061-house-ex-miscellania-do-you-use-these-guys","id":1009061,"title":"House Ex Miscellania - Do You Use These Guys?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-27T15:04:14-08:00","id":1009061,"title":"House Ex Miscellania - Do You Use These Guys?","content":"Been rereading the Order of Hermes Tradition books (original and Revised), and it got me thinking about House Ex Miscellania. Minor Houses like Criamon, Jerbiton, Merinita, etc. I also include the survivors of House Jannisary with this group, after their Revised era purge for secretly being holdovers from the Order of Reason. Groups that expand what it means to be Hermetic (and, in the case of additions from the Ngoma and Wu Lung, just High Ritualist).<br /> <br /> How many of you out there have used Ex Misc Mages in your games, either as PCs or NPCs? And if you haven't, would you want to? What would you do with them if you could?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T18:45:43-08:00","id":1009116,"title":"","content":"I like the House Salad mages, I think they add a lot to the Order and to the games they're in. You can play them as very unique branches of the Order or with the main paradigm with some quirks. Its also got to be a good move for the Order to establish power bases in Africa and China on the native culture's terms, instead of trying to impose their ideas (like the Technocracy is infamous for doing). I also think it'd be interesting to have Ex Miscellanea be just as populous as the major houses, but only House Fortunae realize it.<br /> <br /> <b>Ideas:</b><br /> <br /> -H. Ngoma cabal builds a strong power base in Southern and Eastern Africa by allying itself with pan-Africanism and (oddly enough) the fashion industry in Africa.<br /> <br /> -Members of H. Xaos, desperate for new members, tries to convince/bribe/coerce some H. Fortunae recruiters into sending more acolytes their way. The Fortunae recruiter, thinking the the Xaos mages are speaking for all of Ex Miscellanea, agrees to avoid angering &quot;all of them.&quot;<br /> <br /> -H. Jerbiton, tired of being pushed around as a servant instead of being given the respect a founding house deserves, decides to increase its focus on Ars Spiritus. They reach out to some Dreamspeakers for assistance in securing allies. H. Shaea takes notice.<br /> <br /> -H. Criamon and the new H. Skopos engage in several fruitful (if incomprehensible) debates about the nature of magic and reality. The Riddle-Speakers and Quantum-Hermetics unorthodox perspectives find common ground with each other and shock several Akashics when they discover what one hand clapping really sounds like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T19:02:22-08:00","id":1009123,"title":"","content":"My longest running character yet is from House Merinita, a Kinain mage who's wrapped in the fate of the Arthurian Cycle &amp; is trying to form a grand alliance with those forces that are most harmed by the Consensus (Mages, Fae &amp; Fera, mostly), while ducking the issue of the returning House Diedne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T23:50:22-08:00","id":1009208,"title":"","content":"I played a Criamon on the Path of Strife in Ars Magica. I kind of reincarnated him in a currently running MtSC chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T05:25:53-08:00","id":1009286,"title":"","content":"If a player of mine wants to be in Order of Hermes, then I prefer to match the house to their paradigm of magic, and House Misc. really helps in that regard as the &quot;Well, if nothing else fits&quot; House.<br /> <br /> Just go through one of the many houses in Misc. and see which one fits the most, and then stick them in there as either an offshoot or as someone learning the core values and practises depending on the philosophy of the Mage in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:26:19-08:00","id":1009457,"title":"","content":"Our current Hermetic is (as far as he is concerned) the last scion of House Tharsis (and the descendant of the founder). He had just Awakened was a mere Initiate on his first voyage when the hammer came down and the House was renounced and expelled. He was given a smidge of the benefit of the doubt that he wasn't in on the diabolism yet by the Quaesitori. They slapped him with geasa to keep him away from the sea and Spirit magic, forcibly changed his Shadow Name and sent him to complete his apprenticeship under a mage of House Jerbiton, where he was treated rather poorly and used as a handyman/servant who got to live in the shed out back of the girl's finishing school she was running. He left as soon as he could, but, officially, he's still Ex Misc. and supposed to say &quot;Jerbiton&quot; if pressed.<br /> <br /> Of course, now that he's been gacked from 1902 to 2016, he's started entertaining some pretensions of restoring the honor of his family and House. He's even started using his old Shadow Name again...<br /> <br /> So, that's sort of Ex Misc twice over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}